<article class="env-remark" id="01ZF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01ZF">Remark <span data-tag="01ZF">32.9.2</span>.</a> We cannot do better than this if we do not assume more on $S$ and the morphism $f : X \to S$. For example, in general it will not be possible to find a <em>closed</em> immersion $X \to X'$ as in the lemma. The reason is that this would imply that $f$ is quasi-compact which may not be the case. An example is to take $S$ to be infinite dimensional affine space with $0$ doubled and $X$ to be one of the two infinite dimensional affine spaces. </p>
</article>